The rest of the library, and this edition's own three skills
============================================================

The developer edition's tools page shows three libraries; this one showed one and two empty panels,
because this edition ships the office skills and nothing else. That is not what the page is for — a
tools page with two thirds of it blank reads as broken.

So the published edition now carries what the developer edition carries:

  * the three skills written for this edition — `browser-driving`, `reverse-engineering`, `with` —
    which a previous patch removed. With stays filed under `quixidesk`, because it is Eric Hartford's
    language and this build only packages and documents it.
  * the eleven work skills from a working agent, scrubbed: web-research, post-media-read,
    terminal-email, voice-pipeline, memory-hygiene, local-inference, multi-machine-offload, linux-ops,
    document-extraction, verification-discipline, image-gen-local.
  * the manifest's `owner` values, which is what puts each skill in its panel.

Everything identifying came out of these before they were first shipped: addresses, phone numbers,
mailboxes, given names, a case number, a court, a jurisdiction, LAN addresses, workstation names, home
paths. Delete the identity, keep the measurement.

